      "title": "NotC2: How We Built an AI-Powered C2 Channel With AWS Services",
      "summary": "Varonis Threat Labs built NotC2, a proof-of-concept post-compromise C2 framework that runs entirely on native AWS services and Amazon Bedrock. It assumes the attacker already holds AWS credentials and uses SQS for command input, Lambda for execution, SNS for returning results, and Bedrock to translate natural-language prompts into AWS API calls. Because traffic uses encrypted HTTPS to trusted AWS endpoints with valid credentials, traditional network indicators largely disappear, and the activity appears in the victim's CloudTrail, Lambda, SNS, and Bedrock logs. Defenders are advised to enforce strict IAM least privilege, restrict external SNS subscriptions, and monitor for unusual subscriptions and Bedrock activity under Lambda roles.",
