      "title": "CWPdoor: The Invisible Backdoor Living Inside Control Web Panel",
      "summary": "CWPdoor is a passive backdoor embedded in cwpsrv, the web server for the Control Web Panel (CWP) management interface, and it was analyzed by XLab. Attackers replace the legitimate cwpsrv binary with a recompiled version using a disguised \"version update\" script that also hides file timestamps and command history. The backdoor activates only when it receives a crafted HTTP request with signed, encrypted headers, executes the attacker's commands, and suppresses logging for that request. Mainstream vendors had not detected it at publication, with a zero detection rate on one sample found in a Brazil-uploaded archive. Defenders are advised to check for the integrity Unix socket, rotate control panel credentials, and treat any confirmed host as compromised.",
